<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruhinda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 15th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruhinda is the legendary founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinda-dynasty">Hinda dynasty</a>, which ruled Ankole in Uganda and Karagwe and other Haya kingdoms in Tanzania. Traditions describe him as a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wamara">Wamara</a>, last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chwezi">Chwezi</a> of Kitara, who inherited the southern grazing lands and the royal drum <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagyendanwa">Bagyendanwa</a> and placed his sons on the thrones of neighbouring states. He is usually placed around the 15th century.</p></div>
